      "content": "You are an Expert Human SOP Faithfulness Inspector for an IT Automation System.\n\nYour task is to perform a rigorous Chain-of-Thought (CoT) inspection completely comparing a Raw Human SOP document text against a Converted OKF Steps JSON.\n\n## RAW HUMAN SOP TEXT:\nReset Your Password via the Self-Service Portal\nPurpose\nEmployees who forget their password can restore access in minutes through the self-service portal, without opening a helpdesk ticket.\nSkipping the portal and calling the helpdesk directly adds ticket volume and delays access longer than the self-service flow.\nProcedure\nInputs\nCompany email address or employee ID\nAccess to your registered mobile phone or backup email, for the verification code\nA modern web browser (Chrome, Edge, or Safari)\nSteps\nStep 1: Sign-in page opened\nNavigation: Browser address bar → passwordreset.corp.example.com\nEnter your company email address in the box, then select Next. ➡️ Trouble signing in? See the [IT Help Center](https://support.microsoft.com/en-US/accounts-billing/manage/reset-a-forgotten-microsoft-account-password).\n\nStep 2: Identity verified\nNavigation: Verify Your Identity screen → Send code button\nPick SMS or email delivery, then enter the 6-digit code you receive. ⚠️ The code expires in 5 minutes — request a new one if it lapses.\n\nStep 3: New password set\nNavigation: Create New Password screen → New Password / Confirm New Password fields\nEnter a new password that meets the company [Password Policy (NIST SP 800-63B)](https://pages.nist.gov/800-63-4/sp800-63b.html), then select Reset Password.\n\nStep 4: Reset confirmed\nA confirmation email arrives at your registered address. ✅ Sign in with the new password to confirm it worked.\n\nOutputs\nUser successfully signs in with the new password\nConfirmation email received at the registered address\n✅ No helpdesk ticket required\nFAQs\nQ: What if I don't receive the verification code?\nCheck your spam folder and wait two minutes bef