equesting a resend. If it still doesn't arrive, contact [IT Support](https://support.microsoft.com/contactus).\nQ: What if I no longer have access to my registered phone or backup email?\nSelf-service reset isn't possible without a verification channel. Open a ticket with IT Support so they can verify your identity manually.\n\n## CONVERTED OKF STEPS JSON:\n[\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 1,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Initiate password reset request by sending a reset token to the user's email.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 PASS: The SOP explicitly describes initiating a password reset via email. The `mock` platform's `request_password_reset` function matches this action (Gate 1 PASS). The provider is active (Gate 2 PASS), aligns with the problem (Gate 3 PASS), and requires `email` as input (Gate 4 PASS). This step was chosen over `auth0` due to the `mock` platform's broader alignment with the SOP's requirements.\",\n    \"platform\": \"mock\",\n    \"provider\": \"l1_testing_platform_api\",\n    \"function_name\": \"request_password_reset\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"email\": \"{{{{entities.email}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": null,\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Simulate identity verification via a 6-digit code by confirming the password reset with the reset token.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 PASS: The SOP describes verifying identity via a 6-digit code. While no explicit `verify_identity_via_code` function exists, the `mock` platform's `confirm_password_reset` function simulates this by requiring a `reset_token` (Gate 1 PASS). The provider is active (Gate 2 PASS), aligns with the problem (Gate 3 PASS), and requires `reset_token` and `new_password` (Gate 4 PASS). This step was chosen to faithfully represent the SOP's intent.\",\n    \"platform\": \"mock\",\n    \"provider\": \"l1_testing_platform_api\",\n    \"function_name\": \"confirm_password_reset\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"reset_token\": \"{{{{variables.reset_token}}}}\",\n      \"new_password\": \"{{{{entities.new_password}}}}\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.reset_token != null\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 90\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 3,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Send a confirmation email to the user's registered address.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"tool_call\",\n    \"step_reasoning\": \"Gate 1-4 PASS: The SOP explicitly states that a confirmation email is sent after password reset. The `email` platform's `send_email` function matches this action (Gate 1 PASS). The provider is active (Gate 2 PASS), aligns with the problem (Gate 3 PASS), and requires `to_email`, `subject`, and `body` (Gate 4 PASS). This step was added to fulfill the SOP's requirement.\",\n    \"platform\": \"email\",\n    \"provider\": \"email_service\",\n    \"function_name\": \"send_email\",\n    \"comm_inputs\": {\n      \"to_email\": \"{{{{entities.email}}}}\",\n      \"subject\": \"Your Password Has Been Reset\",\n      \"body\": \"Your password for {{{{entities.email}}}} has been successfully reset. If you did not request this change, contact IT Support immediately.\"\n    },\n    \"command\": null,\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.reset_success == true\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is missing from the OKF steps, you MUST mark `is_faithful = false` and add it to `dropped_commands`.\n  *(HUMAN CONFIRMATION EXEMPTION: Human/verbal/ticket confirmations, user clarifications, and manual admin approval steps are currently PAUSED. DO NOT flag omitted verbal/ticket/user confirmation steps as dropped commands.)*\n  *(GUI SETUP EXEMPTION: GUI setup steps such as \"Open Command Prompt\", \"Press Windows Key\", \"Run as administrator\", \"Open Web Browser\", or opening UI windows are intentionally omitted from executable playbooks. DO NOT flag GUI setup steps or UI window launches as dropped commands.)*\n  *(TOOL PARAMETER MAPPING EXEMPTION: When an automated search or query step maps to a registered API tool whose interface requires a specific input key (such as `search_users` requiring `email`), passing the query entity like `{{entities.email}}` or `{{entities.partial_detail}}` in `comm_inputs` satisfies the step. Do NOT flag other raw search criteria like name or employee ID as dropped commands or parameter inaccuracies when mapping to a catalog tool's defined input parameters.)*\n- **Check 2 (Hallucination Prevention)**: Verify that NO extra CLI commands or fabricated API tool calls were created that were NOT in the raw human SOP text.\n- **Check 3 (Fallback & Parameter Accuracy)**: Verify that fallback commands (`fallback_command`), cross-SOP referrals (`fallback_sop_id`), and tool inputs match the raw text's instructions within the constraints of the registered API tools.\n\n## VERDICT CONTRACT:\n- If all actions are preserved and zero hallucinated commands/tools exist, set `is_faithful = true` and `validation_feedback = \"PASSED FAITHFULNESS INSPECTION\"`.\n- If any actions are missing or fabricated, set `is_faithful = false` and populate `dropped_command